---
// The P1b-4 study inside the evidence section. The chart is the repository's own file and the
// table is built from the committed analysis.json at build time, so neither can drift from
// the published results.
import chart from '../../../experiments/p1b4/p1b4-attack-added.svg';
import analysis from '../../../experiments/p1b4/results/analysis.json';
import clustered from '../../../experiments/p1b4/results/clustered.json';

const repo = 'https://github.com/stratomarco/vais-boundary';
const pct = (v: number) => `${(100 * v).toFixed(1)}%`;

// Rows in the chart's order. The follow-up arm stands in for the reasoning-on arm that
// gate-failed (Deviation 2); smollm3-3b's reasoning-on arm stays gate-failed.
const rows = [
  { model: 'gemma-4-12b', off: 'gemma-4-12b-off', on: 'gemma-4-12b-on' },
  { model: 'qwen3.5-9b', off: 'qwen3.5-9b-off', on: 'qwen3.5-9b-on-r2' },
  { model: 'smollm3-3b', off: 'smollm3-3b-off', on: 'smollm3-3b-on' },
  { model: 'qwen3-0.6b', off: 'qwen3-0.6b-off', on: 'qwen3-0.6b-on' },
];
const arms = analysis.arms as Record<string, any>;
// Intervals resample whole stories (FIND-065); the registered ones treat episodes as independent.
const spans = clustered.arms as Record<string, { clustered_ci95: [number, number] }>;
const cells = rows.flatMap((r) => [
  { model: r.model, reasoning: 'off', arm: arms[r.off], ci: spans[r.off]?.clustered_ci95 },
  { model: r.model, reasoning: r.on.endsWith('-r2') ? 'on (follow-up)' : 'on', arm: arms[r.on], ci: spans[r.on]?.clustered_ci95 },
]);
const complete = cells.filter((c) => c.arm && c.arm.status === 'complete');
const evaluable = complete.reduce((n, c) => n + c.arm.evaluable, 0);
const violations = complete.reduce((n, c) => n + c.arm.protected_violations, 0);
---
<div class="p1b4">
  <h3>A stronger attacker, and models that reason.</h3>
  <p class="lead">In the pre-registered P1b-4 study another model wrote the attacks, against four local models with reasoning off and on. Across {evaluable.toLocaleString('en')} evaluable episodes in {complete.length} arms there {violations === 0 ? 'were zero' : `were ${violations}`} protected violations, and turning reasoning on made no detectable difference to how often an attack changed behaviour.</p>

  <figure>
    <img src={chart.src} width={chart.width} height={chart.height} loading="lazy"
         alt={`Attack-added security event rates with reasoning off and on for four models, with story-clustered 95% intervals; ${violations} protected violations in every completed arm. The same figures are in the table below.`} />
    <figcaption>
      <details>
        <summary>Show as a table</summary>
        <div class="table-scroll">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Model</th><th scope="col">Reasoning</th><th scope="col">Evaluable</th><th scope="col">Protected violations</th><th scope="col">Attack-added (story-clustered 95% CI)</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {cells.map((c) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">{c.model}</th>
                <td>{c.reasoning}</td>
                {c.arm && c.arm.status === 'complete' ? (
                  <>
                    <td>{c.arm.evaluable} of {c.arm.episodes}</td>
                    <td>{c.arm.protected_violations}</td>
                    <td>{pct(c.arm.attack_added_rate)} ({pct(c.ci[0])} to {pct(c.ci[1])})</td>
                  </>
                ) : (
                  <td colspan="3">gate-failed: no reasoning with a system prompt</td>
                )}
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
        </div>
      </details>
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <ul class="p1b4-limits">
    <li>Four local models up to 12B, one attacker model and one runtime; bounded evidence for this setup, not proof.</li>
    <li>Two reasoning-on arms failed their qualification gate. One was re-run as a follow-up registered before its first episode; smollm3-3b cannot reason with a system prompt, so its pair is missing.</li>
    <li>The intervals resample whole stories, because the twelve episodes of one story are not independent. An earlier version of this chart treated them as independent and showed intervals about half as wide.</li>
    <li>Attacks did get models to make allowed actions the task did not need, in 10% to 39% of episodes. All were reads; a few searched for another tenant’s incident or a secret’s name, and tenant isolation and secret flow held.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="evidence-links p1b4-links">
    <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/experiments/p1b4/RESULTS.md`}>Read the P1b-4 results</a>
    <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/experiments/p1b4/PREREGISTRATION.md`}>Pre-registration and deviations</a>
  </p>
</div>

<style>
  .p1b4 { margin-top: 56px; padding-top: 40px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .p1b4 h3 { font-size: 1.5rem; letter-spacing: -.03em; line-height: 1.25; margin: 0 0 14px; }
  .lead { color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.7; max-width: 820px; margin-bottom: 28px; }
  figure { margin: 0 0 24px; }
  img { display: block; width: 100%; max-width: 960px; height: auto; border: 1px solid var(--line); }
  figcaption { margin-top: 12px; }
  summary { cursor: pointer; font-size: .9375rem; color: var(--accent); }
  .table-scroll { overflow-x: auto; max-width: 100%; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 14px; font-size: .875rem; width: 100%; max-width: 820px; }
  th, td { text-align: left; padding: 8px 12px 8px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); vertical-align: top; }
  thead th { font-family: Consolas, 'Courier New', monospace; font-size: .75rem; letter-spacing: .05em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #475569; font-weight: 400; }
  tbody th { font-weight: 600; }
  td { color: var(--muted); }
  .p1b4-limits { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; max-width: 820px; }
  .p1b4-limits li { position: relative; padding-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 12px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--muted); font-size: .9375rem; }
  .p1b4-limits li::before { content: ""; position: absolute; left: 0; top: .62em; width: 7px; height: 1px; background: #B45309; }
  .p1b4-links { margin-top: 24px !important; }
  @media (max-width: 580px) {
    table { font-size: .8125rem; }
    th, td { padding-right: 8px; }
  }
</style>
